{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Data opt-out to include the NHS Federated Data Platform and associated NDIT",
        "additional_details": "Patients should be given a fuller explanation of the NHS architecture and its planned use of patient data so an informed decision can be made on the opt-out. This should include how AI is used within this architecture and the extent to which UK data protection laws cover the data held.\r\n\r\nThis opt-out should include all further expansion of the NHS data architecture so that the system-wide architecture that links the patient identifier to other systems should also be subject to the same opt out. \r\n",
        "background": "When patients choose to opt out using the NHS 'opt-out', this should always include opting out of the Federated Data Platform (FDP) and the National Data Integrated Tenant (NDIT).",
